# Run artefacts, not source. These are rebuilt on demand and some are large:
# archive-blobs.txt is a full listing of the container (~350k lines, tens of MB) and
# archive-tails.txt is the index derived from it. Both are caches keyed by mtime.
archive-blobs.txt
archive-tails.txt
allblobs*.txt

# One CSV per reconciler run, plus the scheduled task's logs.
missed-reconcile-*.csv
reconcile-logs/

# One CSV per orphan scan.
index-orphans-*.csv
index-unbacked-*.csv

# CLIENT CORRESPONDENCE - none of the below may ever be committed.
#
# purged-documents-*.json holds the FULL BODY TEXT of messages whose index rows were
# removed; it exists precisely because deleting those rows destroyed the last record of
# them. messageid-index.tsv maps 258,974 RFC 5322 Message-IDs to matter paths, i.e. who
# corresponded about which matter. older-mail-*.csv carries subjects and message ids.
#
# These were committed once, on 2026-08-30, because a `git reset --hard` during a PR split
# silently reverted this file and took the patterns with it. Caught before pushing. If the
# ignore rules ever look thinner than expected, suspect exactly that.
purged-documents-*.json
messageid-index.tsv
older-mail-*.csv
archive-items.txt
tree.txt
